  ## Notes

  [bold]Paygrade equivalence[/bold]: Ranks with the same paygrade are considered equivalent in authority for MP purposes
  [bold]Special ranks[/bold]: Some factions have special ranks (Commissars, Specialists) that may not have direct equivalents
  [bold]Aviation ranks[/bold]: Some factions have separate aviation tracks (WeYu, PSC)
  [bold]Administrative ranks[/bold]: Corporate factions may have administrative ranks without military equivalents
  [bold]Unique paygrades[/bold]: Corporate factions (PSC, VAI, LB) use unique paygrade systems that don't directly map to military O/W/E grades
  [bold]Synthetic ranks[/bold]: Some factions have dedicated synthetic rank tracks (PSC, VAI)

  ## Usage for Military Police

  When dealing with personnel from different factions:
  1. Identify their rank and paygrade
  2. Use this table to find the equivalent rank in your faction
  3. Apply appropriate protocols based on the equivalent authority level

  Example: A UPP Marshal (O10) has equivalent authority to an RMC General (O10) or US Army General (O10).

  For corporate factions with unique paygrade systems, use judgment based on the role description (e.g., "Director" typically has high authority, "Associate" is entry-level).
